Fill the entire background with one flat, uniform, fully opaque pure magenta, RGB 255 0 255, hex #FF00FF, edge to edge. The background must be that exact single colour and nothing else: no grey-and-white checkerboard pattern, no white, no grey, no gradient, no texture, no vignette, no ground plane, no cast shadow, no glow or halo bleeding into it. Magenta appears nowhere on the subject itself. Use a landscape canvas exactly twice as wide as it is tall (2:1 aspect ratio, for example 2048x1024).

Game status-effect icon sprite for a 2.5D faceted low-poly papercraft game, matching the exact rendering technique of the attached reference images.

Rendering technique, required exactly as in the references:
- Build every shape from flat polygonal facet planes, like cut and folded paper. One flat, completely solid color per plane. Hard, sharp creases between adjacent planes.
- No smooth 3D shading, no soft gradient across a plane, no gloss, no specular highlight, no surface texture, no surface grain, no photographic noise, no painterly brushwork, no airbrush, no glow, no bloom.
- If the result could be mistaken for a rendered 3D model, a photo, or a digital painting, it is wrong. It must look built from cut and folded matte paper facets.
- One soft light source from the upper left of EACH shape: a broad flat highlight facet on the upper-left side of every shard, a broad flat shadow facet on the lower-right side. Nothing else.
- No outer contour line and no ink outline anywhere. Shapes separate from each other only by flat color value.
- Restrained saturation, mid-to-high value. Nothing muddy, nothing neon.

Two-frame layout, required exactly:
- The canvas is split by an invisible vertical line exactly at its horizontal midpoint into two equal square panels: a LEFT panel (frame 1) and a RIGHT panel (frame 2). Do not draw the dividing line, a border, a seam, or any frame around either panel — it stays implied only by empty magenta.
- Frame 1 and Frame 2 show the exact same subject, drawn at the exact same overall scale and the exact same overall bounding size, centered the same way inside its own panel. Keep every shard at least 10% of the panel width away from the vertical midline and from the panel's outer edges, so nothing crosses the seam and nothing touches the border.
- The ONLY differences allowed between Frame 1 and Frame 2: each shard is rotated in place by a small angle (5 to 15 degrees, some clockwise, some counter-clockwise, never uniform), each shard shifts position by only a tiny amount (at most 4% of the panel width, to suggest a crackling jitter), and the highlight/shadow split on a shard may shift slightly to suggest a flicker. The overall silhouette size, the overall bounding box, and the hollow empty center MUST stay identical between the two panels. Never make Frame 2's cluster larger, smaller, or shifted off-center compared to Frame 1 — this exact mistake (a 10% size mismatch between the two frames) is what sank three earlier attempts at this asset.

Subject identity, shared by both frames: a SHOCKED / ELECTROCUTED status-effect marker that will be composited above a creature sprite in-game — never as a background element, always as a small floating overlay icon. Five separate small forked-lightning-bolt shard fragments, each a jagged zigzag bolt silhouette (like a stylized lightning-bolt icon, NOT a crystal or gem shape), built from 3 to 4 flat facet planes per bolt. Vary the five bolts' sizes noticeably — a couple of larger bolts, a couple of smaller ones, one tiny fragment. Scatter them loosely around a completely empty center in an irregular, asymmetric ring — never a perfect radial star, never mirror-symmetric, never touching or overlapping each other. The empty center must stay clear so a creature drawn underneath this icon remains readable. Palette: highlight #FCFBD5, main gold #F6DB5F, deep gold #D7A313, dark amber shadow #996B07 — use only these four colors, one flat color per facet.

Exclusions: no crystal, no gem, no diamond shapes, no cloud, no rain drop, no circle ring, no closed loop, no card border, no icon plate, no dish, no coin shape, no text, no frame, no watermark, no logo, no creature, no face. Silhouette of each bolt must stay clearly readable when shrunk to 64 pixels wide.
